{
  "context": "Introduce `benchbox/utils/clock.py` with explicit separation of concerns:\nmonotonic elapsed timing (`mono_time`, `elapsed_seconds`, stopwatch/context)\nand wall-clock event timestamps (`utc_now`).\n\nUpdate correctness hotspots first, with targeted tests:\n- Replace perf_counter-to-datetime conversion bug in core results timing.\n- Replace timeout arithmetic in lock/poll loops with monotonic elapsed checks.\n- Keep persisted event timestamps in UTC wall clock where semantically required.\n",
  "description": "Build the timing foundation for BenchBox runtime code by introducing a shared\nclock utility and fixing correctness-critical timing bugs discovered during\nadversarial review.\n\nThis item covers the first implementation phase:\n1) Create centralized monotonic/wall-clock helpers in a reusable module.\n2) Fix the monotonic-to-wall-clock timestamp bug in core timing collection.\n3) Convert high-risk timeout/retry loops to monotonic elapsed logic.\n4) Migrate MCP benchmark elapsed calculations to monotonic timing.\n5) Stabilize resource-rate elapsed calculations with monotonic deltas.\n\nThis phase is intentionally scoped to correctness and foundation APIs so later\ntiming migrations can proceed with low ambiguity and low regression risk.",
